    "permalink": "https://sarveda.com/store/sound-musical-instruments/indian-classical/annapurna-shankh/",
    "sku": "",
    "short_description": "<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"378\" data-end=\"706\">Traditionally placed in homes, temples and altars, the Shankh is regarded as an auspicious symbol of prosperity, nourishment and spiritual well-being.</p>\n<p data-start=\"708\" data-end=\"999\">With its naturally sculpted spiral form, distinctive ridges and warm ivory tones, each shell showcases the unique artistry of nature. The Shankh can also be blown to produce a <strong data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"908\">deep, resonant sound</strong>, making it a meaningful addition to puja, aarti, meditation and other spiritual practices.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1001\" data-end=\"1221\">Traditionally sounded during <strong data-start=\"1030\" data-end=\"1083\">pujas, aartis, festivals and auspicious occasions</strong>, the resonant tone of the conch is considered spiritually significant and is believed to help create a purified and uplifting atmosphere.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1223\" data-end=\"1469\">Beyond its ceremonial use, the Annapurna Shankh makes an elegant <strong data-start=\"1288\" data-end=\"1367\">decorative piece for home altars, meditation spaces and spiritual interiors</strong>. As a natural shell, every piece will have its own variations in shape, colour, texture and markings.</p>",
    "description": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"382\" data-end=\"402\">Annapurna Shankh</strong> is a naturally formed conch shell valued in Hindu tradition for its association with <strong data-start=\"488\" data-end=\"554\">Annapurna Devi, the goddess of food, nourishment and abundance</strong>.</p>",
