  {
    "id": 51251,
    "name": "Sughosh Shankh \u2013 Natural Conch Shell",
    "slug": "sughosh-shankh-natural-conch-shell",
    "parent": 0,
    "type": "simple",
    "variation": "",
    "permalink": "https://sarveda.com/store/sound-musical-instruments/indian-classical/sughosh-shankh-natural-conch-shell/",
    "sku": "",
    "short_description": "<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"57\" data-end=\"385\">Its name comes from the Sanskrit word <em data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"247\">Sughosh</em>, associated with a <strong data-start=\"267\" data-end=\"307\">beautiful or auspicious proclamation</strong>, reflecting the clear, penetrating sound traditionally produced by the conch.</p>\n<p data-start=\"387\" data-end=\"694\">The shell shown features a naturally sculpted, robust form with prominent ridges, organic textures and warm <strong data-start=\"495\" data-end=\"535\">cream, golden and earthy brown tones</strong>. Its substantial structure and naturally formed contours give it a striking presence, while every shell remains unique in shape, colour, markings and texture.</p>\n<p data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"1018\">Traditionally blown during <strong data-start=\"723\" data-end=\"782\">pujas, aartis, festivals and other auspicious occasions</strong>, the Sughosh Shankh is used to mark the beginning of rituals and create a resonant sound within sacred spaces. In Hindu tradition, the Sughosh Shankh is also associated with <strong data-start=\"957\" data-end=\"967\">Nakula</strong>, one of the Pandava brothers in the <em data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1017\">Mahabharata</em>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1020\" data-end=\"1248\">Beyond ceremonial use, this natural conch makes a beautiful addition to <strong data-start=\"1092\" data-end=\"1159\">temples, home altars, meditation spaces and spiritual interiors</strong>, combining traditional significance with the organic beauty of a naturally formed shell.</p>",
    "description": "<p>Naturally formed by the ocean, the <strong data-start=\"92\" data-end=\"110\">Sughosh Shankh</strong> is a distinctive natural conch traditionally valued for its powerful and resonant voice.</p>",
