    "permalink": "https://sarveda.com/store/sound-musical-instruments/indian-classical/gaumukhi-shankh-natural-conch-shell/",
    "sku": "",
    "short_description": "<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"58\" data-end=\"389\">Its broad, naturally sculpted form and characteristic opening are associated with the gentle face of <strong data-start=\"330\" data-end=\"359\">Gau Mata (the sacred cow)</strong>, giving this Shankh its name.</p>\n<p data-start=\"391\" data-end=\"614\">The shell features beautiful natural ridges, spiral formations and warm ivory, cream and subtle brown tones. Every piece has its own unique shape, markings and surface texture, reflecting the natural formation of the shell.</p>\n<p data-start=\"616\" data-end=\"893\">Traditionally used during <strong data-start=\"642\" data-end=\"703\">puja, aarti, meditation, prayer and auspicious ceremonies</strong>, the Gaumukhi Shankh can be blown to produce a deep, resonant sound. In traditional practice, the sound of the conch is believed to create an uplifting and spiritually purifying atmosphere.</p>\n<p data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"1262\">Also known as <strong data-start=\"909\" data-end=\"930\">Panchmukhi Shankh</strong> in some traditions, it is commonly kept in homes, temples and spiritual spaces as an auspicious object associated with <strong data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1100\">peace, harmony, prosperity and positive energy</strong>. Beyond its ceremonial use, its naturally sculptural form makes it a beautiful decorative piece and a meaningful gift for spiritual practitioners and collectors.</p>",
    "description": "<p>Naturally formed by the ocean, the <strong data-start=\"93\" data-end=\"112\">Gaumukhi Shankh</strong> is a distinctive natural conch shell traditionally valued for its auspicious appearance and spiritual significance.</p>",
